  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "S2 contains no numeric permanent limit and no sales stop: the 5% figure is only a reporting and corrective-action trigger, and the regulator may impose restrictions but is not required to, so the Hearth 10 cannot be forced off the market. S5 makes an 8/100k recall mandatory with no interim window and a 'promptly' notice, which directly bears on the Ember 8 at 9.9/100k, although the remedy is left to the regulator. S3 (6-year retrofit) and S4 (36 months) sit inside the acceptable ranges, and S1 is strict (24-hour reporting covering all thermal events)."
